  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "The unified specification uses only task-level delivery actions, color observations, claim coordination, pickup and delivery outcomes, and matching delivery publication events. It omits low-level movement and obstacle events because search_object, approach_object, search_zone, and approach_zone provide the required mission-level motion and collision_avoidance already protects that motion.",
    "transition_design": "object_search repeatedly enables search_object and selects a red, green, or blue branch only after the corresponding object-visible observation. Each claim-attempt state enables only its matching claim and abandons on the matching received-claim, received-delivered, or not-visible observation. A successful claim enters an object-approach state immediately. Object and zone search or approach actions are repeatable self-loops, not-visible observations return to the relevant search state, and reached observations permit pickup or drop from either search or approach. Pickup and delivery failures restart the appropriate phase, while delivery confirmation requires the matching publication before delivery_complete. pick_up_object and drop_object are excluded from all states except their corresponding reached checkpoints.",
    "feedback_response": "No previous-run feedback was supplied."
